## Task
Rooms already support country/state/city in the data model and in `search_groups()` — see "what already exists" below. Finish wiring: the `/api/groups` route needs to read/pass those fields, and the rooms page needs UI to set and filter by them.

## What already exists (verified — do not reimplement)
- `src/lib/server/group.ts`: `Group.co/st/ci`, `GroupView.country/state/city`, `save_group`/`update_group` accept `{country?, state?, city?}`, `search_groups(env, q, loc?, limit)` filters correctly with or without a query.
- `src/lib/LocationPicker.svelte`: reusable `bind:country bind:region bind:city` picker, `showCity` toggle, `anyLabel` prop. Already used in `src/routes/app/+page.svelte` (people search filters, `showCity={false}`) and `src/routes/app/profile/+page.svelte` (`showCity` default true).
- `src/routes/app/rooms/[id]/+page.svelte` already DISPLAYS `g.city`/`g.state`/`g.country` in the "about this room" modal (line ~334) — it just has no way to set them.

## Phase 1 — write the tests

### `/api/groups` route — `src/routes/api/groups/__tests__/server.test.ts` *(new file — this route has none yet; follow the mocking pattern in `src/routes/api/push/__tests__/server.test.ts`: mock `$env/dynamic/private` and `$lib/server/group`)*
- `it('401s when signed out')` for GET and POST
- `it('passes country, state and city query params through to search_groups')`
- `it('plain-lists with list_groups when there is no query and no location filters')`
- `it('persists country, state and city on create')` — POST body includes them, assert `save_group` was called with them

### `/api/groups/[id]` PATCH — `src/routes/api/groups/[id]/__tests__/server.test.ts` *(check if it exists; extend or create)*
- `it('persists country, state and city on update')`

### Rooms page — `src/routes/app/rooms/__tests__/page.svelte.test.ts` *(new — component-render test: name it `*.svelte.test.ts` so the jsdom `component` vitest project picks it up; for a bindable prop use a `*Host.test.svelte` wrapper, see `src/lib/components/__tests__/ModalHost.test.svelte`)*
- `it('offers a location picker in the create-room modal')`
- `it('hides location filters until the filter icon is clicked')` (mirror `src/routes/app/+page.svelte`'s `filtersOpen`/`SlidersHorizontal` pattern)
- `it('sends country and state on room search')`
- `it('shows the location under a room name when set')`
- `it('shows no location line for a room without one')`

## Phase 2 — watch them fail
`pnpm test` — all new tests fail (route params ignored today; no picker in the page).

## Phase 3 — implement

**`src/routes/api/groups/+server.ts`:**
```ts
export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ url, locals }) => {
	if (!locals.user) throw error(401, 'auth');
	if (url.searchParams.get('mine')) return json({ r: await list_groups(env, locals.user.id) });
	const q = url.searchParams.get('q')?.trim() ?? '';
	const country = url.searchParams.get('country')?.trim() || undefined;
	const state = url.searchParams.get('state')?.trim() || undefined;
	const city = url.searchParams.get('city')?.trim() || undefined;
	if (!q && !country && !state && !city) return json({ r: await list_groups(env) });
	return json({ r: await search_groups(env, q, { country, state, city }) });
};

export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, locals }) => {
	if (!locals.user) throw error(401, 'auth');
	const b = (await request.json().catch(() => null)) as {
		name?: string; description?: string; country?: string; state?: string; city?: string;
	};
	const name = b?.name?.trim();
	if (!name) throw error(400, 'name required');
	return json({
		g: await save_group(env, locals.user.id, {
			name, description: b?.description, country: b?.country, state: b?.state, city: b?.city
		})
	});
};
```
Check `search_groups`'s actual current parameter shape in `group.ts` before writing this (it is `search_groups(env, q, loc?, limit)` where `loc` is `{country?, state?, city?}` — confirm the param name/shape in `group.ts` matches what's called here).

**`src/routes/api/groups/[id]/+server.ts`:** PATCH handler passes `country`, `state`, `city` from body through to `update_group`, same as name/description already are.

**`src/routes/app/rooms/+page.svelte`:**
- Add `country`/`region`/`city` `$state` and a `filtersOpen` state + `SlidersHorizontal` icon button next to "find rooms", copying the exact pattern from `src/routes/app/+page.svelte` lines ~34-38, 99-113, 115-155 (activeFilterCount badge, `<Modal>` with `<LocationPicker>`, clear/apply buttons).
- `search()` appends `country`/`state`/`city` to the querystring.
- The "start a room" `<Modal>` (line ~146) gains `<LocationPicker bind:country bind:region bind:city anyLabel="country" />` and `create()` includes them in the POST body.
- Each result `<li>` (line ~100) and each "your rooms" `<li>` (line ~178) shows `{#if g.city || g.state || g.country}<div class="text-[12px] text-mute">{[g.city, g.state, g.country].filter(Boolean).join(' · ')}</div>{/if}` under the name, matching the style already used in `src/routes/app/+page.svelte` lines ~179-187.

**`src/routes/app/rooms/[id]/+page.svelte`:** the owner edit form (line ~310-325) gains the same `<LocationPicker>`, and `save_edits()`'s PATCH body includes `country`/`state`/`city`.

## Phase 4 — watch them pass
`pnpm test` all green, `pnpm check` clean. Commit as `room-location-ui`, then `plan.ts plan room-location-ui`.

credits-graceful-degradation.step_details:
## Task
Fix `GET /api/credits` 500ing (seen live in `.dev-logs/server.log`: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'W', "Worker "x2"... is not valid JSON`).

## Root cause
`src/lib/server/credit_client.ts`'s `get_balance()` calls `res.json()` unconditionally on whatever `locals.x2_ws.fetch(...)` returns, with no check of `res.ok` and no try/catch. When the `x2-ws` Worker isn't reachable on the expected port (e.g. `pnpm dev:ws` not running alongside `pnpm dev`, so `devFetcher()`'s hardcoded `http://localhost:8787` hits nothing useful, or in production if the DO service binding ever has a transient failure), the response body is plain text, not JSON — `.json()` throws a raw `SyntaxError` that isn't caught anywhere, and SvelteKit turns it into an unhandled 500. Compare with `src/routes/api/search/+server.ts`'s `presence()`, which already treats a failed downstream call as a soft `null` ("couldn't check, show everyone") instead of throwing. `credit_client.ts` should follow the same convention: downstream failure is a degraded state, not a crash — the profile page (`src/routes/app/profile/+page.svelte`) already renders `credit_balance === null ? '—' : ...`, i.e. it already expects "no data yet" to be silently possible.

## Phase 1 — write the tests
**File:** `src/lib/server/__tests__/credit_client.test.ts` *(new — mock the `Fetcher` passed in, not `$env` — this module takes its `ws: Fetcher` as a plain argument, no Qdrant/env involved)*
- `it('returns the parsed balance when the ws worker responds with JSON')`
- `it('returns a null/zero-balance fallback instead of throwing when the response body is not JSON')`
- `it('returns a null/zero-balance fallback instead of throwing when fetch itself rejects')` (network error / connection refused)

**File:** `src/routes/api/credits/__tests__/server.test.ts` *(existing — check it, extend)*
- `it('returns a 200 with a degraded balance instead of 500 when the ws worker is unreachable')`

## Phase 2 — watch them fail
`pnpm test` — new tests fail (current code throws instead of degrading).

## Phase 3 — implement
In `src/lib/server/credit_client.ts`, wrap the JSON parse:
```ts
async function safe_json<T>(res: Response, fallback: T): Promise<T> {
	if (!res.ok) return fallback;
	try {
		return (await res.json()) as T;
	} catch {
		return fallback;
	}
}

export async function get_balance(ws: Fetcher, uid: string): Promise<Balance> {
	try {
		const res = await call(ws, `/credits/${uid}/balance`);
		return await safe_json(res, { balance: 0, granted_today: false });
	} catch {
		return { balance: 0, granted_today: false };
	}
}
```
Apply the same `try { ... } catch { return fallback }` shape to `deduct()` and `credit()` — pick sensible fallbacks for each (`deduct` should probably fall back to `{ ok: false, reason: 'insufficient_credits', balance: 0 }` so a caller never treats an unreachable ws worker as a successful deduction). Check every caller of `deduct`/`credit` (grep for them) to make sure a fallback `ok:false` doesn't cause a worse user-facing error than today's crash — if any caller needs to distinguish "actually insufficient" from "couldn't reach ws", add a distinct reason instead of reusing `insufficient_credits`.

## Phase 4 — watch them pass
`pnpm test` all green. Read `.dev-logs/server.log` after this change is live — confirm no new `[500] GET /api/credits` lines appear even if the ws worker isn't running. Commit as `credits-graceful-degradation`, then `plan.ts plan credits-graceful-degradation`.
